   "id": "crush-diagnostics-md-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "# Errors and Diagnostics\n\n> Verified against crush-ast `bad81048` (v0.9.0, 2026-10-31).\n\nThis page is about how the tools *report* a problem; the language's own\n`try`/`catch`/`throw` is in [Control Flow](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/control_flow.html#errors-try--catch--throw).\nSince 0.9.0 `crush`, `crushc` and `crush-run` report problems with one JSON schema,\nand a semantic error points at the line and column it is on.\n\n## Text (the default)\n\nA mistake the compiler can see is reported before anything runs:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-diagnostics-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    let x = 1\n    print(y)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
